    "tessercheck_runs_count": 10,
    "final_message": "The red acceptance test now passes. `RESTATE_INGRESS=http://localhost:38380 RESTATE_ADMIN=http://localhost:39370 STORY_DRAFTING_PORT=9330 scripts/verify story-drafting` is green: tessercheck with zero findings, `mypy --strict` clean, 75 tests pass in the other tiers, and the root acceptance test passes against the served host. It's committed as `aba6b3f` on `baseline/runs/green-v2-3`; nothing was pushed.\n\n**What a run does now.** `POST /runs` starts the `RunOrchestrator` workflow, which:\n1. saves the run with stage `drafting`;\n2. drafts stories through a new `DrafterActions` activity, behind a `StoryDrafter` port;\n3. saves the run again with those stories and stage `awaiting_pick`;\n4. waits on a durable promise named `pick_stories`.\n\n`GET /runs/{id}` then shows `awaiting_pick`, the drafted stories, and no accepted stories. Nothing resolves the promise yet, because making the pick is out of scope.\n\n**Acceptance test:** `story-drafting/tests/test_story_drafting.py` is unchanged from the red commit, in setup and in assertions.\n\n**Choosing the drafter.** The component takes a drafter setting:\n- `canned` is a deterministic drafter that builds stories from the job text.\n- `anthropic` calls `claude-opus-5-5` for structured JSON output.\n- An absent or unknown value, or `anthropic` without a key, fails when the app starts.\n\nThe app reads `STORY_DRAFTING_DRAFTER` and `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` from the environment. In `scripts/verify`, only `run_story_drafting` changed: it always sets `canned`, so a leftover environment variable can't make the gate call a real model.\n\n**Changes to existing behaviour:**\n- **Repository saves:** the in-memory repository now replaces a saved run instead of keeping the first one. The run has to be saved a second time to record its stories, and I updated that repository test to match.\n- **Existing workflow and dispatcher tests:** the run now waits instead of finishing. So these tests check the journal up to the wait and then end the waiting run in Restate"
  },
